{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review 1 BLOCKED on 3 real gaps, all verified against the code: (a) _llm_error_exit_code printed its message only for retryable outcomes, so a now-non-retryable refusal surfaced nothing on the raised-error path; (b) close_gate_remedy maps any CHANGE_SETTINGS to the install-the-extra remedy (already handled in the first commit, now also tested end to end through _raise_close_failure, with a distinct PROXY_REFUSED_REMEDY so the close error does not repeat the hint); (c) model_classes.should_fall_back would stop the fallback chain at a proxy-refused primary; it now still advances, since a refusal is per host. Also: the group diagnostic carries the legs' distinct proxy texts, and docs/config.md names the refusal under CHANGE_SETTINGS. Plan updated; review 2 PASS (signed). Amended as 2a99872bfc4 (same Change-Id); 17 new tests and 402 existing tests on the changed paths pass. make verify run 1 discarded: the worktree changed under it. Rerun started 03:22 PST."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795432930428619001,"uuid":"43ae605c-9272-426b-81e4-6d08f1525519"}